---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import { polyline } from '../geometry';
import { pageLang } from '../../../utils/lang';

const ru = pageLang(Astro.url) === 'ru';

// Three observations, so that y lives in R³ and can be drawn: x = (0, 1, 2), y = (1, 3, 2), columns 1 and x.
// The normal equation gives ŵ = (1.5, 0.5), ŷ = (1.5, 2, 2.5) and the residual (−0.5, 1, −0.5), orthogonal to both
// columns. Any other fit Xw is farther from y: for w = (1, 1), ‖y − Xw‖² = 2 = 1.5 + 0.5 (Pythagoras).
type V3 = [number, number, number];
const dot = (a: V3, b: V3) => a[0] * b[0] + a[1] * b[1] + a[2] * b[2];
const sub = (a: V3, b: V3): V3 => [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]];
const mul = (k: number, a: V3): V3 => [k * a[0], k * a[1], k * a[2]];
const norm = (a: V3) => Math.sqrt(dot(a, a));
const x1: V3 = [1, 1, 1], x2: V3 = [0, 1, 2], y: V3 = [1, 3, 2];
const g = [[dot(x1, x1), dot(x1, x2)], [dot(x2, x1), dot(x2, x2)]], c = [dot(x1, y), dot(x2, y)];
const det = g[0][0] * g[1][1] - g[0][1] * g[1][0];
const w = [(g[1][1] * c[0] - g[0][1] * c[1]) / det, (g[0][0] * c[1] - g[1][0] * c[0]) / det];
const yhat: V3 = [0, 1, 2].map((i) => w[0] * x1[i] + w[1] * x2[i]) as V3;
const r = sub(y, yhat);
const xw: V3 = [0, 1, 2].map((i) => x1[i] + x2[i]) as V3; // w = (1, 1)
const rss = dot(r, r), rssOther = dot(sub(y, xw), sub(y, xw)), gap = dot(sub(yhat, xw), sub(yhat, xw));
if (w.map((v) => v.toFixed(2)).join() !== '1.50,0.50' || Math.abs(dot(r, x1)) + Math.abs(dot(r, x2)) > 1e-12) throw new Error('ProjectionGeometry: the fit drifted from the note');
if (rss.toFixed(2) !== '1.50' || rssOther.toFixed(2) !== '2.00' || gap.toFixed(2) !== '0.50') throw new Error('ProjectionGeometry: distances drifted from the note');
// An orthonormal frame: u1, u2 span the column space, nrm is the direction of the residual.
const u1 = mul(1 / norm(x1), x1);
const t2 = sub(x2, mul(dot(x2, u1), u1)), u2 = mul(1 / norm(t2), t2);
const nrm = mul(1 / norm(r), r);
const coords = (v: V3) => [dot(v, u1), dot(v, u2), dot(v, nrm)] as V3;
const id = 'projection-geometry';
const t = ru
  ? { col: 'col(X)', y: 'y = (1, 3, 2)', yhat: 'ŷ = Xŵ = (1.5, 2, 2.5)', r: 'y − ŷ ⊥ x₁, x₂', rs: '‖y − ŷ‖² = 1.5', xw: 'Xw, w = (1, 1)', other: '‖y − Xw‖² = 2 = 1.5 + 0.5', x1: 'x₁ = 1', x2: 'x₂ = x' }
  : { col: 'col(X)', y: 'y = (1, 3, 2)', yhat: 'ŷ = Xŵ = (1.5, 2, 2.5)', r: 'y − ŷ ⊥ x₁, x₂', rs: '‖y − ŷ‖² = 1.5', xw: 'Xw, w = (1, 1)', other: '‖y − Xw‖² = 2 = 1.5 + 0.5', x1: 'x₁ = 1', x2: 'x₂ = x' };
const tn = { y: 'y', yhat: 'ŷ', r: 'y − ŷ', xw: 'Xw', x1: 'x₁', x2: 'x₂' };
const layouts = [
  { cls: 'fig-wide', W: 760, H: 236, s: 92, o: [110, 196], short: false },
  { cls: 'fig-narrow seq-narrow', W: 360, H: 170, s: 52, o: [52, 140], short: true },
];
const draw = (L: (typeof layouts)[number]) => {
  const P = (v: V3) => { const [a, b, cc] = coords(v); return [L.o[0] + L.s * (a + 0.5 * b), L.o[1] - L.s * (0.33 * b + cc)] as [number, number]; };
  const Q = (a: number, b: number) => [L.o[0] + L.s * (a + 0.5 * b), L.o[1] - L.s * 0.33 * b] as [number, number];
  const plane = polyline([Q(-0.4, -0.7), Q(4.2, -0.7), Q(4.2, 1.75), Q(-0.4, 1.75), Q(-0.4, -0.7)]) + ' Z';
  const k = 0.2;
  const dirIn = mul(1 / norm(sub(xw, yhat)), sub(xw, yhat));
  const box = polyline([P([0, 1, 2].map((i) => yhat[i] + k * nrm[i]) as V3), P([0, 1, 2].map((i) => yhat[i] + k * nrm[i] + k * dirIn[i]) as V3), P([0, 1, 2].map((i) => yhat[i] + k * dirIn[i]) as V3)]);
  return { P, plane, box, O: P([0, 0, 0]), Y: P(y), Yh: P(yhat), Xw: P(xw), X1: P(x1), X2: P(x2), colAt: Q(0.05, 1.35) };
};
---

<Figure
  id={id}
  title={ru ? 'Метод наименьших квадратов как проекция' : 'Least squares as a projection'}
  caption={ru
    ? 'Три наблюдения, x = (0, 1, 2), y = (1, 3, 2), модель ŷ = w₁ + w₂x. Вектор y лежит в R³, а все возможные прогнозы Xw заполняют плоскость col(X), натянутую на столбцы x₁ = (1, 1, 1) и x₂ = (0, 1, 2). Решение нормального уравнения ŵ = (1.5, 0.5) даёт основание перпендикуляра из y на плоскость: остаток (−0.5, 1, −0.5) ортогонален обоим столбцам. Любая другая точка плоскости дальше: для w = (1, 1) квадрат расстояния 2 = 1.5 + 0.5 по теореме Пифагора.'
    : 'Three observations, x = (0, 1, 2), y = (1, 3, 2), and the model ŷ = w₁ + w₂x. The vector y lives in R³, and all possible predictions Xw fill the plane col(X) spanned by the columns x₁ = (1, 1, 1) and x₂ = (0, 1, 2). The solution of the normal equation, ŵ = (1.5, 0.5), gives the foot of the perpendicular from y to the plane: the residual (−0.5, 1, −0.5) is orthogonal to both columns. Every other point of the plane is farther: for w = (1, 1) the squared distance is 2 = 1.5 + 0.5, by Pythagoras.'}
>
  {layouts.map((L) => {
    const D = draw(L);
    return (
      <svg class={L.cls} viewBox={`0 0 ${L.W} ${L.H}`} role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-${L.W}-t ${id}-${L.W}-d`}>
        <title id={`${id}-${L.W}-t`}>{ru ? 'Проекция вектора ответов на пространство столбцов' : 'Projection of the response vector onto the column space'}</title>
        <desc id={`${id}-${L.W}-d`}>{ru ? 'Плоскость, натянутая на два столбца матрицы признаков; над ней точка y; вертикальный остаток опускается в точку ŷ под прямым углом; пунктир от y к другой точке плоскости Xw длиннее.' : 'A plane spanned by the two feature columns; the point y above it; the residual drops vertically to ŷ at a right angle; a dashed segment from y to another point Xw of the plane is longer.'}</desc>
        <path d={D.plane} class="f-fill-blue" style="stroke: var(--fig-blue); stroke-opacity: .5; stroke-width: 1" />
        <text class="f-small f-t-blue" x={D.colAt[0]} y={D.colAt[1]}>{t.col}</text>
        <path class="f-line" d={`M ${D.O[0]} ${D.O[1]} L ${D.X1[0]} ${D.X1[1]}`} marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
        <path class="f-line" d={`M ${D.O[0]} ${D.O[1]} L ${D.X2[0]} ${D.X2[1]}`} marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
        <text class="f-small" x={D.X1[0] - 4} y={D.X1[1] + 18} text-anchor="middle">{L.short ? tn.x1 : t.x1}</text>
        <text class="f-small" x={D.X2[0] - 10} y={D.X2[1] - 8} text-anchor="end">{L.short ? tn.x2 : t.x2}</text>
        <circle cx={D.O[0]} cy={D.O[1]} r="2.5" class="f-solid-muted" />
        <text class="f-note" x={D.O[0] - 6} y={D.O[1] + 15} text-anchor="end">0</text>
        <path class="f-line f-muted f-dash" d={`M ${D.Y[0]} ${D.Y[1]} L ${D.Xw[0]} ${D.Xw[1]}`} />
        <path class="f-thin f-muted" d={`M ${D.Yh[0]} ${D.Yh[1]} L ${D.Xw[0]} ${D.Xw[1]}`} />
        <path class="f-line f-red f-bold" d={`M ${D.Y[0]} ${D.Y[1]} L ${D.Yh[0]} ${D.Yh[1]}`} />
        <path class="f-thin" d={D.box} />
        <circle cx={D.Y[0]} cy={D.Y[1]} r="4" class="f-solid-green" />
        <circle cx={D.Yh[0]} cy={D.Yh[1]} r="4" class="f-solid-blue" />
        <circle cx={D.Xw[0]} cy={D.Xw[1]} r="3.5" class="f-solid-muted" />
        <text class="f-label f-t-green" x={D.Y[0] + 10} y={D.Y[1] - 6}>{L.short ? tn.y : t.y}</text>
        <text class="f-small f-t-blue f-halo" x={D.Yh[0] - 8} y={D.Yh[1] + 20} text-anchor="end">{L.short ? tn.yhat : t.yhat}</text>
        <text class="f-small f-t-red f-halo" x={D.Y[0] - 8} y={D.Y[1] + 24} text-anchor="end">{L.short ? tn.r : t.r}</text>
        {!L.short && <text class="f-note f-halo" x={D.Y[0] - 8} y={D.Y[1] + 41} text-anchor="end">{t.rs}</text>}
        <text class="f-small f-halo" x={D.Xw[0] + 9} y={D.Xw[1] + 5}>{L.short ? tn.xw : t.xw}</text>
        {!L.short && <text class="f-note f-halo" x={D.Xw[0] + 9} y={D.Xw[1] + 23}>{t.other}</text>}
      </svg>
    );
  })}
</Figure>
